      <link>http://www.nupi.no/en</link>
      <description><![CDATA[<div class="content" id="list_item_frontpage_16_9"><div class="list_item list_item_frontpage_16_9 item"><div class="card_details"><div class="component_primary_tag">Articles</div><div class="card_item"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="none" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" width="24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M3 6H21V21H3V6Z" stroke="#222222"></path><path d="M3 11L21 11" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"></path><path d="M9 16H15" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="square"></path><path d="M8 3L8 7" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"></path><path d="M16 3L16 7" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg><time datetime="2026-06-28">June 28, 2026</time></div></div><div class="main_content"><div class="left_container"><h2 class="list_title"><a href="/en/news/how-do-diplomats-work-with-technology" title="How do diplomats work with technology?">How do diplomats work with technology?</a></h2><p class="abstract"> A new study could shape how diplomats follow AI in the years ahead. </p></div><a aria-hidden="" class="image_container" href="/en/news/how-do-diplomats-work-with-technology" tabindex="-1" title="How do diplomats work with technology?"><figure class=""><picture><source srcset="https://www.nupi.no/var/nupi/storage/images/_aliases/scaledown210_180/0/0/8/5/1265800-6-eng-GB/decab1f00fb7-Medium-2-1-.jpg 1x"/><img alt="" loading="lazy" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7"/></picture></figure></a></div></div><div class="list_item list_item_frontpage_16_9 item"><div class="card_details"><div class="component_primary_tag">Articles</div><div class="component_secondary_tag"> New research </div><div class="card_item"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="none" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" width="24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M3 6H21V21H3V6Z" stroke="#222222"></path><path d="M3 11L21 11" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"></path><path d="M9 16H15" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="square"></path><path d="M8 3L8 7" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"></path><path d="M16 3L16 7" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg><time datetime="2026-06-23">June 23, 2026</time></div></div><div class="main_content"><div class="left_container"><h2 class="list_title"><a href="/en/news/climate-peace-and-security-fact-sheet-lake-chad" title="Climate, Peace and Security Fact Sheet: Lake Chad*">Climate, Peace and Security Fact Sheet: Lake Chad*</a></h2><p class="abstract"> The ongoing insecurity in the Lake Chad region—which intersects Cameroon, Chad, Niger and Nigeria—cannot be understood in isolation from climate and environmental change. </p></div><a aria-hidden="" class="image_container" href="/en/news/climate-peace-and-security-fact-sheet-lake-chad" tabindex="-1" title="Climate, Peace and Security Fact Sheet: Lake Chad*"><figure class=""><picture><source srcset="https://www.nupi.no/var/nupi/storage/images/_aliases/scaledown210_180/2/6/4/5/1265462-1-eng-GB/0a928fbc8a0e-Skjermbilde-2026-06-23-kl.-13.08.42.png 1x"/><img alt="Skjermbilde 2026-06-23 kl. 13.08.42.png" loading="lazy" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7"/></picture></figure></a></div></div><div class="list_item list_item_frontpage_16_9 item"><div class="card_details"><div class="component_primary_tag">Articles</div><div class="component_secondary_tag"> New research </div><div class="card_item"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="none" height="24" viewbox="0 0 24 24" width="24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M3 6H21V21H3V6Z" stroke="#222222"></path><path d="M3 11L21 11" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"></path><path d="M9 16H15" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="square"></path><path d="M8 3L8 7" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"></path><path d="M16 3L16 7" stroke="#222222" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg><time datetime="2026-06-11">June 11, 2026</time></div></div><div class="main_content"><div class="left_container"><h2 class="list_title"><a href="/en/news/why-ai-and-automation-do-not-equal-better-security" title="Why AI and Automation Do Not Equal Better Security">Why AI and Automation Do Not Equal Better Security</a></h2><p class="abstract"> AI and machine learning are widely assumed to deliver better cybersecurity. But human experience and judgement remain deeply embedded in detecting and countering digital threats, according to a new article. </p></div><a aria-hidden="" class="image_container" href="/en/news/why-ai-and-automation-do-not-equal-better-security" tabindex="-1" title="Why AI and Automation Do Not Equal Better Security"><figure class=""><picture><source srcset="https://www.nupi.no/var/nupi/storage/images/_aliases/scaledown210_180/8/0/6/3/1263608-1-nor-NO/12d1a2a9973b-169_Nytt-varslingssystem-cyberangrep_Foto-Ronja-S-Larsen_Aftenposten_NTB.jpg 1x"/><img alt="169_Nytt varslingssystem cyberangrep_Foto Ronja S Larsen_Aftenposten_NTB.jpg" loading="lazy" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7"/></picture></figure></a></div></div></div>]]></description>
